    [Feature][MRV2] Default encoder-decoder models to Model Runner V2 (#19159)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Unset `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER` still selects Model Runner V1 when
    `is_encoder_decoder` is true. Whisper is that blacklist entry.
    Encoder-decoder model state on MRV2 is already on main (#17979, #18044),
    so this PR drops the entry. Explicit `0` or `1` still wins. Pooling,
    310P, and the other blacklist entries are unchanged.
    
    `test_whisper` was skipped only because it selected V1. The skip is
    removed.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. With the env unset, encoder-decoder models use Model Runner V2. Set
    `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=0` to keep V1.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `tests/ut/test_mrv2_utils.py`: `encoder-decoder` moved to the
    default-V2 cases.
    - Skip removed from
    `tests/e2e/pull_request/one_card/test_vlm.py::test_whisper`
    (`openai-mirror/whisper-large-v3-turbo`).
    - The same case already passed on A2 with V2 forced: [job
    116506795563](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38731662735/job/116506795563).
    This PR lets CI run it with the env unset.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
